      <p class="ssb-aeo-text">
        According to the Social Security Administration (SSA), retirement benefits are calculated using your 35 highest-earning years adjusted for inflation (Average Indexed Monthly Earnings, or AIME). In 2026, the Primary Insurance Amount (PIA) formula replaces <strong class="ssb-gold">90% of the first $1,226/month</strong>, <strong class="ssb-gold">32% between $1,226 and $7,391</strong>, and <strong class="ssb-gold">15% above $7,391</strong>. The average monthly check for retirees in 2026 is approximately $1,976.
